\f0\fs24 \cf0 Different models. Same ideas.\
\
We tested 5 LLMs across 2 topics and 3 prompt types.  \
No matter how we changed the inputs, the outputs consistently collapsed into the same small set of patterns.\
\
Setup\
\
- Models: GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek, Claude, Grok  \
- Topics: Elderly Mobility, Education  \
- Prompt Types:\
  - Open\
  - Constrained\
  - Cross-domain  \
\
Total: 30 conditions tested\
\
Key Finding\
\
Across all models and conditions, ideas consistently mapped to 6 structural patterns:\
\
- Optimization\
- Platform / System\
- Social Systems\
- Network / Flow\
- Environmental Design\
- Tech Integration\
\
What Changes vs What Stays Constant\
\
What changes:\
- Wording\
- Tone\
- Metaphors (biological, technical, social)\
\
What stays constant:\
- Core idea structure\
- Pattern types\
- System-based logic\
\
Why this matters\
\
LLMs appear creative at the surface level, but operate within a constrained conceptual space.  \
The diversity is mostly in language \'97 not in underlying ideas.\
